{"toolCallId":"call_f76fbcdde410431cacf67e764d683399","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"026-graph-and-context-optimization\n027-xce-research-based-refinement\n028-memory-search-intelligence\n029-spec-root-resolution-hardening\n031-memory-reindex-embed-performance\n032-relocate-specs-folder\n033-system-speckit-v4\n034-spec-folder-tooling\n035-retire-memory-era-tests\n040-goal-parent-single-limit\n041-write-recipe-fixes\n046-align-runtime-code-with-sk-code-skilled\n047-plugin-scanner-readiness\n048-doctor-command-audit\n049-doctor-audit-followups\n050-open-knowledge-format-adoption\n051-symlinked-runtime-root\n052-research-folder-continuity\n053-ci-workflow-efficiency\ndescription.json\n=== validate help ===\nvalidate.sh - Spec Folder Validation (v3.0.0)\n\nUSAGE: ./validate.sh <folder-path> [OPTIONS]\n\nOPTIONS:\n    --help, -h     Show help     --version, -v  Show version\n    --json         JSON output   --strict       Run strict-only rules\n    --verbose      Detailed      --quiet, -q    Results only\n    --recursive    Validate parent + all [0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/ child phase folders\n    --no-recursive Disable auto-recursive validation when phase children exist\n\nENVIRONMENT:\n    SPECKIT_RULES              Comma-separated subset of rules to evaluate\n    SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION    1, true, yes or on skips validation (also read from hook-flags.env)\n    SPECKIT_STRICT/_VERBOSE/_JSON/_QUIET   Equivalent to the flags above\n\nEXIT CODES: 0=pass, 1=user error, 2=validation error, 3=system error\n\nRULES BY CATEGORY:\n  authored_template:\n    FILE_EXISTS [error] - Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\n    PLACEHOLDER_FILLED [error] - Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\n    COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER [error] - Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\n    SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED [error] - Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\n    STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY [error] - Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\n    LEVEL_DECLARED [info] - Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\n    AC_COVERAGE [info] - Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\n    AC_CLOSURE [error] - Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\n    ANCHORS_VALID [error] - Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\n    FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK [error] - Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\n    SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY [error] - Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\n    TOC_POLICY [error] - Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\n    AI_PROTOCOLS [error] - Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\n    COMPLEXITY_MATCH [error] - Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\n    FOLDER_NAMING [error] - Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\n    FRONTMATTER_VALID [error] - Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\n    FRONTMATTER_VALUES [warn] - Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\n    SOURCE_TAGS [warn] - Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\n    GREP_CONVENTION [error] - Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\n    LEVEL_MATCH [error] - Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\n    SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY [error] - Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\n    TEMPLATE_SOURCE [error] - Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\n  operational_runtime:\n    MERGE_LEGALITY [error] - Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\n    CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION [error] - Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\n    POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT [error] - Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\n    GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT [warn] - Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\n    GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT [warn] - Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\n    NORMALIZER_LINT [error] - Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\n    CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED [error] - Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\n    CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED [error] - Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\n    CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED [error] - Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\n    CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED [error] - Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\n    CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS [error] - Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\n    CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS [error strict-only] - Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\n    LINKS_VALID [warn] - Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n  structural:\n    GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY [error] - Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\n    GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE [warn] - Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\n    METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY [error] - Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"37f992","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
